---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../../components/Disclaimer.astro';

const UPDATED = '28 July 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Disclaimer | Save My Gig!"
  description="Save My Gig gives free general guidance on DJ storage and player problems. It is provided as is, without warranty, and you follow it at your own risk."
  path="/legal/disclaimer"
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="status-line">LEGAL</div>
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:2rem">Last updated: {UPDATED} · Part of <a href="/legal">the legal shelf</a></p>

    <Disclaimer variant="full" />

    <h2 class="dsc-sec">What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      Save My Gig is a free resource written by a working DJ. It offers general
      guidance on common problems with DJ storage devices, media players and
      library software. It is published in good faith and for general
      information only.
    </p>

    <h2 class="dsc-sec">No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      All content is provided <strong>"as is"</strong>, without warranty of any
      kind, express or implied. We do not warrant that the information is
      accurate, complete, current, or suitable for your particular hardware,
      firmware, software version or situation. Manufacturers change firmware and
      software behaviour without notice, and a step that worked yesterday may
      not work today.
    </p>

    <h2 class="dsc-sec">Risk of data loss</h2>
    <p>
      Some procedures described on this site, including formatting, erasing,
      repartitioning, re-exporting and overwriting storage devices, will
      <strong>permanently destroy data</strong>. Data destroyed this way is
      normally unrecoverable without professional assistance, and sometimes not
      at all. You are solely responsible for backing up your files before you
      begin, and for confirming that you are operating on the correct device.
    </p>

    <h2 class="dsc-sec">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Save My Gig, its owner and its
      contributors accept <strong>no liability whatsoever</strong> for any loss
      or damage of any kind arising out of or in connection with the use of this
      site or reliance on its content. This includes, without limitation: loss
      or corruption of data, music libraries, playlists, cue points or metadata;
      damage to storage devices, players, computers or other equipment; missed,
      interrupted or cancelled performances; and any direct, indirect,
      incidental, consequential or economic loss, including loss of income or
      reputation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in this disclaimer excludes or limits liability where it would be
      unlawful to do so.
    </p>

    <h2 class="dsc-sec">Not professional data recovery</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not a substitute for professional data recovery. If the files
      on your drive are irreplaceable, stop using the drive immediately and
      consult a qualified data recovery service. Continuing to use, re-mount or
      format a failing drive can reduce or eliminate the chance of recovery.
    </p>

    <h2 class="dsc-sec">Third parties, hardware and links</h2>
    <p>
      References to manufacturers, products, software and services are for
      identification and guidance only. We are not affiliated with, endorsed by,
      or acting on behalf of AlphaTheta, Pioneer DJ, or any other manufacturer
      or software vendor named on this site. All trademarks belong to their
      respective owners.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some links to products or services may be affiliate links, meaning we may
      earn a commission at no additional cost to you. This never changes what we
      recommend, and there are no affiliate or sponsored links inside the
      emergency rescue flow.
    </p>

    <h2 class="dsc-sec">Your responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      By using this site you confirm that you understand the risks described
      above, that you are acting on your own judgement, and that you accept full
      responsibility for the outcome. If you are not comfortable with that, do
      not follow the steps, and seek professional help instead.
    </p>

    <h2 class="dsc-sec">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this disclaimer:
      <a href="mailto:savemygig@gmail.com">savemygig@gmail.com</a>, or use the
      <a href="/feedback">feedback form</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .dsc-sec { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.7rem; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  main p { color: var(--text-dim); }
  main p strong { color: var(--text); }
</style>
